// Underground room templates (exploration-and-sites 3.1, P4-H): cellars, crypts and tombs of ruined churches, abbeys and keeps.
// Characters: # wall, . floor, + door (where a corridor joins), < stairs up, > stairs down, H shaft or ladder down, o pillar or prop (a support),
// $ loot spot, n burial niche (named dead), b bier or bed, ^ trap spot, l light sconce, ~ water, : rubble, v ore face.
// CI (test EX-3): every row the same width, every floor reachable from a door or portal, every purpose known.
[
  { "type": "site_room", "id": "stairs_down", "purposes": ["entrance"], "rows": [
      "#####",
      "#.<.#",
      "#...#",
      "#l..#",
      "##+##" ] },
